# SPDX-License-Identifier: CC-BY-4.0
#
# The EXACT output of the native producer math::producers::r_lift (dogfooded — this
# fixture IS what the producer emits, byte for byte after the SPDX header block).
# r_lift runs the shipped executable R front-end, gmeow_math_lift::r::lift — the same
# entrypoint the `gmeow` CLI calls — over the real committed artifact
# crates/math-lift/fixtures/mtcars.R, embedded in the binary at compile time, and mints
# under the producer namespace. Nothing here is hand-authored: every triple was derived
# by the recursive-descent R parser and its lift tier.
#
# The run is a math:RIngestRun carrying the four ingest-frame obligations (a retained
# logic:loadBearing math:parseSource witness, logic:instantiatesSchema,
# logic:instantiatesPlan, and a math:ingestCorrespondence whose logic:Correspondence
# holds the whole law spine), and a structured math: codomain of 103 nodes, each
# gmeow:wasGeneratedBy the run — a non-empty lift, clean under math:UnliftableIngest.
# The rung is an honest lossy lens over a VAGUE source (logic:LossyLens /
# logic:ValidationOnly / logic:RelatedMatch / logic:Vague, logic:mnemomorphic true):
# R's general computation and control flow do not survive into math:.
#
# Drift is a loud failure: crates/math/tests/lift_fixture_drift.rs regenerates the
# producer and byte-compares against this file.

